## THE TICKET (MPSCALC-359, Backlog, 1 comment, labels lane-v4, mpscalc-b1082, plan-b1082-t2, tier-1; Jira GET at drafting; QUOTED)
Summary: "perSite: a component quantity counted per site of a purchase group". Recommendation: "add perSite after the sites work lands, with a register row and a red-first test for a quantity counted per site of the group; an unknown rule stays refused and the three rules of MPS #137 stay unchanged." **Acceptance check: "perSite has a register row and a red-first test for a quantity per site; a group of several sites counts the component once per site; an unknown rule is still refused; the three rules of MPS #137 are unchanged."** Where: `src/MpsCalc.Engine/Input/PurchaseInput.cs` (the rule member), `src/MpsCalc.Engine/Calculation/PurchaseCalculator.cs` and `src/MpsCalc.Engine/Reconciliation/PurchaseRecomputation.cs` (the count), `docs/ENGINE.md` (the register rows beside X-40 to X-42), `tests/MpsCalc.Engine.Tests/ComponentQuantityRuleTests.cs`. Its dependency, the sites work, is MPSCALC-257 (Done, landed). **The ticket Where has no Api, contract or web path: those are separate work (MPSCALC-358 is the Api half of the three existing rules).**

## WHAT "A perSite LINE" IS TODAY, AND WHAT THE RULING NEEDS (MEASURED by the drafter at the pin; this is the point of the kit)
- **There is no perSite line in the product.** The rule is the enum `ComponentQuantityRule` with three members: `PurchaseInput.cs:40` (`public enum ComponentQuantityRule`), `PerDevice` `:43`, `FixedPerGroup` `:45`, `Manual` `:47`. A case-insensitive search for `persite` over `src`, `web/src`, `docs` and `tests` at the pin prints exactly four lines: `docs/ENGINE.md:166` and `:169` (both say perSite is not a member), `tests/MpsCalc.Api.Tests/QuoteApiTests.QuantityRule.cs:24` (the string `"perSite"` as a spelling the Api refuses) and `tests/MpsCalc.Engine.Tests/ComponentQuantityRuleTests.cs:633` (`string[] names = ["PerSite", "UsageOnly"];`, names that "cannot be read"); control: `InvalidSiteAllocation` prints 2 lines in `src`.
- **So the refusal cannot be built without the line.** This kit therefore adds the member `PerSite` (the engine's own spelling, a fourth member appended as value 3, so stored numbers keep their meaning, as `ItemClass.CarePack` was) and the count the ticket asks for. The count is the ticket's "once per site", with the ruling's "count sites with at least one device": **a `PerSite` line counts its typed quantity times S, where S = the number of the section's sites that hold at least one device** (`Devices` 1 or more; a site of 0 devices is not counted). The group's fleet quantity N is not read for the count. (The report's Q-1 asks Tuesday to confirm this reading; it is the one place this kit reads the ticket's words with the ruling's words together.)
- **Where the sites are.** `PurchaseSection.Sites` is `IReadOnlyList<SiteAllocation>?` (`PurchaseInput.cs`, the record `SiteAllocation(string Site, int Devices)`); the structure check for it is `PurchaseCalculator.cs:333`-`:340` (`if (s.Sites is { Count: > 0 } allocation)`, blocks with `PurchaseRules.InvalidSiteAllocation`, its text at `:338`); an empty or absent list raises nothing (`docs/ENGINE.md:169`). The Review check `CheckSiteAllocation` is `:578`, called at `:216`.
- **Where the line is counted today.** `PurchaseCalculator.cs:181` extends a per-device line of a group to `n * l.Quantity` (`checked`) and leaves every other rule as typed; `:203`-`:205` set `QuantityPerDevice` for a per-device line only; every later count reads the extended line. The structure check of a line is the loop at `:370`, the unknown-rule refusal `:389`-`:392` (`if (!Enum.IsDefined(l.QuantityRule))`, `Block(PurchaseRules.InvalidQuantityRule, ...)`, the `Block` helper at `:310`), the result carries the rule at `:621`. The reconciler counts at `PurchaseRecomputation.cs:50`-`:52` (`groups`, `QuantityOf`) and `:68`. **A member that nothing reads is counted as typed (like `Manual`)**, which is why commit A is inert and commit B's rows are red on it.
- **Reachability (for Tuesday, not for you to fix).** `src/MpsCalc.Api` holds `FleetQuantity` on 0 lines (control: `QuantityRule` 19 lines) and builds no site (its two `Sites` hits are the rental fleet label, `Proposal.cs:429` and `:447`); `web/src` names `quantityRule` on 0 non-test, non-generated lines (control: the generated `schema.ts` names it 2 times). So no quote made through the Api or the screens can state a group, a site or this rule: the new note is reached by the engine only, today. That is the reason this kit stops at the engine, and why the Api half (the member on the contract, groups and sites on the request) and the note's place on a screen are later changes (report Q-2, Q-5).

